    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d365">

                <pb facs="0646" n="512" sameAs="frus:frus1888p1/pg512"/>

                <head>No. 365.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. McLane to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-02-16"><hi rendition="#italic">February</hi> 16, 1888</date>.
                        (Received February 27.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 551.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Your No. 272 of November 18 communicated to
                    me, at the request of the Postmaster General, two copies of a printed memorial,
                    signed by prominent American merchants,<anchor n="*" xml:id="d365-f1"/>
                    suggesting the propriety <pb facs="0647" n="513" xml:id="pg513"/> of the general
                    adoption of the policy of dispatching all foreign mails by the fastest steamers.
                    In the interest of the facilitation of commercial intercourse I was directed to
                    bring this memorial to the notice of the French Government, and I did so
                    immediately upon receiving it. I am now in possession of a note from Mr.
                    Flourens stating, in behalf of the French postal department, that the policy
                    referred to is the one followed by that department.</p>
                <p>I inclose a copy and translation of Mr. Flourens’s note herewith.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert M. McLane.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d365-a1.xml" xpointer="d365-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
